    %% ---- Help text -----------------------------------------------------------
    %% What `%%entity … help:` and `%%field … help:` buy: they are compiled into
    %% sys_table.description and sys_column.description, which are the only help
    %% the generated application has — the tooltip beside a control, and the lede
    %% of that entity's section in the generated manual. A model without them
    %% produces an application whose every field is a label somebody guesses at.

    %%entity User help: Someone who signs in and does the work — a rep, a manager, an agent. Every business record names one as its owner.
    %%entity Team help: A group of users under one manager, carrying a shared quota. Teams are how sales targets roll up.
    %%entity Territory help: A slice of the market — a region, a country, a company-size band — that accounts are assigned to.
    %%entity Account help: A company you sell to or support. Almost everything else in this application hangs off an account.
    %%entity Contact help: A person at an account. Contacts are who you talk to; accounts are who you invoice.
    %%entity Lead help: An unqualified enquiry that has not been connected to an account yet. A lead is either converted into an account, a contact and an opportunity, or disqualified.
    %%entity Campaign help: A marketing programme with a budget and a window, run to generate leads.
    %%entity CampaignMember help: One person on one campaign's target list, and whether they responded.
    %%entity Opportunity help: A deal in progress against an account, with an amount, a stage and a close date. The pipeline is the sum of these.
    %%entity OpportunityLineItem help: One product on one opportunity, priced. The opportunity's amount is what these add up to.
    %%entity OpportunityLineItem parent: Opportunity
    %%entity Product help: Something you sell, with a list price. Products are what line items point at.
    %%entity Quote help: A priced, versioned offer to an account for one opportunity. A quote is what gets approved and sent.
    %%entity QuoteLineItem help: One product on one quote, priced, in the order it appears on the document.
    %%entity QuoteLineItem parent: Quote
    %%entity Contract help: The signed commitment that follows an accepted quote — a term, an annual value and a renewal date.
    %%entity SupportCase help: A customer problem, from the moment it arrives to the moment it is resolved, measured against an SLA.
    %%entity SlaPolicy help: How quickly cases must be answered and resolved for a given tier of customer.
    %%entity Activity help: A call, a meeting, an email or a task, attached to whatever it was about. The history of a relationship is its activities.

